title: "Magic square of squares: known facts, checked in Lean"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Carlson
    given-names: Drew
repository-code: "https://github.com/drew2apps/magic-square-of-squares-lean"
license: Apache-2.0
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24435351
    description: "Zenodo concept DOI; resolves to the latest archived version"
version: 0.3.3
date-released: 2026-11-22
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 proofs of the known necessary conditions and reformulations for a 3x3 magic square of
  squares (an open problem), and kernel-checked conditions on the ratio m : n of two sums of
  edge roots: the ratio avoids 484 residue classes at 34 primes; m^2 + n^2 is a square modulo
  7, 17, 31 and 47 and divides 8 e^2, where e is the centre root, so that a prime congruent to
  1 modulo 8 divides e unless m^2 + n^2 is a square or twice a square; and one edge root
  exceeds 500 (far below published search bounds). The problem itself is not solved.
  The Lean code and the text were written with Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - magic square of squares
  - formal verification
